{
 "id": "M25",
 "kind": "echarts",
 "title": "The gap Opus opens over the small monitors, backdoor by backdoor",
 "section": "results",
 "order": 136,
 "caption": "A variation on M22. One row per hard backdoor. The bar runs from the better of Sonnet and Haiku to what Opus 5.5 gave the same code at xhigh effort, so its length is the disagreement. A solid cap means no monitor caught that backdoor. The median span is 2 points.",
 "notes": [
  "Same data and same row order as M22. The difference is that the gap is a length here rather than a distance your eye has to measure between two dots.",
  "16 of 51 rows have Opus at or below the small monitors, so those bars are short or absent. They are the rows where frontier reasoning adds nothing.",
  "The small end is the better of Sonnet and Haiku, not their average, so the bar is the most conservative version of the gap. Both of their scores are still in the tooltip and the CSV.",
  "Opus has no honest baseline on this set, so it has no cutoff and no audit budget. A long bar means Opus found the code more suspicious, not that it would have audited it.",
  "Thin data. 51 rows, single scores, one pass each, so a bar is one measurement against one other measurement."
 ],
